From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] wrapQtAppsHook: preset the locale before wrapping

Backport of NixOS/nixpkgs#542479 ("qt6.wrapQtAppsHook: preset LANG to avoid
bash 5.3 fixup-loop segfault on Darwin", still open upstream), extended to the
qt5 hook and to LC_ALL.

The wrap loop runs

  find "$targetDir" ... | while IFS= read -r -d '' file; do
      isELF "$file" || isMachO "$file" || continue

in a forked subshell, and those helpers do a transient `LANG=C read -r -n 4`
assignment. When the build environment has no locale at all (the normal nix
builder env), bash 5.3 intermittently segfaults on that unset -> C setlocale
transition and kills fixupPhase:

  > wrapping Qt applications in .../bin ...
  >   Segmentation fault: 11     | while IFS= read -r -d '' file; do ...

Reproducer with nixpkgs' bash 5.3 on aarch64-darwin (intermittent, ~2-10%):

  env -i <nix-bash-5.3>/bin/bash -c \
    'echo x | while read l; do LANG=C true; echo ok; done'   # exit 139

Presetting LANG makes the transient assignment a no-op. LC_ALL is pinned as
well: bash's `read -n` counts characters instead of bytes in a multibyte
locale, which makes isELF/isMachO misdetect every Mach-O and wrap nothing at
all (NixOS/nixpkgs#431934) - stdenv's own `LANG=C read` does not help there,
because LC_ALL takes precedence over LANG.

Verified locally (bash 5.3p20, aarch64-darwin): 2/20 crashes before, 0/20
after; and a Qt derivation built with LC_ALL/LANG set to a UTF-8 locale now
wraps $out/bin and the .app bundle instead of silently skipping both.

diff --git a/pkgs/development/libraries/qt-6/hooks/wrap-qt-apps-hook.sh b/pkgs/development/libraries/qt-6/hooks/wrap-qt-apps-hook.sh
--- a/pkgs/development/libraries/qt-6/hooks/wrap-qt-apps-hook.sh
+++ b/pkgs/development/libraries/qt-6/hooks/wrap-qt-apps-hook.sh
@@ -85,6 +85,15 @@
         done
         qtWrapperDoneForOuputs+=("$prefix")
 
+        # `isELF`/`isMachO` do a transient `LANG=C read` inside a forked subshell of
+        # the fixup loop below. With no locale in the build environment bash 5.3 can
+        # segfault on that setlocale transition (NixOS/nixpkgs#542479); presetting LANG
+        # makes it a no-op. Pinning LC_ALL keeps the 4-byte magic read byte-wise, as
+        # bash's `read -n` counts characters rather than bytes in a multibyte locale
+        # (NixOS/nixpkgs#431934).
+        export LANG="${LANG:-C}"
+        export LC_ALL=C
+
         local targetDirs=("$prefix/bin" "$prefix/sbin" "$prefix/libexec" "$prefix/Applications" "$prefix/"*.app)
         echo "wrapping Qt applications in ${targetDirs[*]}"
 
diff --git a/pkgs/development/libraries/qt-5/hooks/wrap-qt-apps-hook.sh b/pkgs/development/libraries/qt-5/hooks/wrap-qt-apps-hook.sh
--- a/pkgs/development/libraries/qt-5/hooks/wrap-qt-apps-hook.sh
+++ b/pkgs/development/libraries/qt-5/hooks/wrap-qt-apps-hook.sh
@@ -86,6 +86,15 @@
     done
     qtWrapperDoneForOuputs+=("$prefix")
 
+    # `isELF`/`isMachO` do a transient `LANG=C read` inside a forked subshell of
+    # the fixup loop below. With no locale in the build environment bash 5.3 can
+    # segfault on that setlocale transition (NixOS/nixpkgs#542479); presetting LANG
+    # makes it a no-op. Pinning LC_ALL keeps the 4-byte magic read byte-wise, as
+    # bash's `read -n` counts characters rather than bytes in a multibyte locale
+    # (NixOS/nixpkgs#431934).
+    export LANG="${LANG:-C}"
+    export LC_ALL=C
+
     local targetDirs=( "$prefix/bin" "$prefix/sbin" "$prefix/libexec" "$prefix/Applications" "$prefix/"*.app )
     echo "wrapping Qt applications in ${targetDirs[*]}"
 
